# Paths the document-deslop skill never runs on.
#
# One repo-relative path, directory, or glob per line; a directory covers its
# whole subtree; `**` matches any number of directories, including none; `!`
# prefixes an exception that stays due; `#` opens a comment line. Every entry
# carries a comment saying why. Unlike .deslopped, an entry here records no
# sha: exemption is permanent and does not lapse when the file changes.

# The catalog the skill reads to do its job. Every `**Before** "..."` in it is
# a deliberate specimen of a tic, so an agent applying the standard to this
# file would destroy the examples that define it.
standards/prose/slop-tics.md

# Indexes. Each entry restates the frontmatter `description` of the file it
# links, and okf-lint fails the commit when the two drift. The description is
# the target file's to change, so an index is never rewritten on its own.
**/index.md

# READMEs. A README is the landing doc for a directory — an H1 and a one-line
# purpose, per standards/docs/readme-content.md. Six of the seven run 9-45
# lines, too small to carry a tic.
**/README.md

# Except this one, which has outgrown the landing-doc shape at 197 lines and
# carries real prose.
!scripts/README.md

# Vendored skills. Everything under an `.agents/` path is a third-party skill
# carried unmodified so it can be re-synced from upstream; its voice is its
# author's to set, per standards/prose/conventions.md.
dotfiles/.agents/**

# Decision Records. A Decision Record is a dated account of a past decision —
# the alternatives rejected, the context that forced it — and is never
# rewritten to match later state. Removing changelog residue from one would
# destroy the point of the document.
docs/decisions/**

# Frozen skills. A `frozen-` skill is a point-in-time copy held for the factory
# rebuild, and its references/ mirror docs whose live originals are deslopped
# separately. A style pass would break the freeze.
dotfiles/dot-claude/skills/frozen-*/**
